1706248"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["21706248"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["11621063"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["11621063"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100002367","name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["QYZDB\u2010SSW\u2010SLH018"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["QYZDB\u2010SSW\u2010SLH018"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100002367","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100002858","name":"China Postdoctoral Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["BH2310000033"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["BH2310000033"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100002858","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Advanced Materials"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2018,5]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Developing highly efficient catalysts for oxygen evolution reaction (OER) in neutral media is extremely crucial for microbial electrolysis cells and electrochemical CO\n                    <jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>\n                    reduction. Herein, a facile one\u2010step approach is developed to synthesize a new type of well\u2010dispersed iridium (Ir) incorporated cobalt\u2010based hydroxide nanosheets (nominated as CoIr) for OER. The Ir species as clusters and single atoms are incorporated into the defect\u2010rich hydroxide nanosheets through the formation of rich Co\u2013Ir species, as revealed by systematic synchrotron radiation based X\u2010ray spectroscopic characterizations combining with high\u2010angle annular dark\u2010field scanning transmission electron microscopy measurement. The optimized CoIr with 9.7 wt% Ir content displays highly efficient OER catalytic performance with an overpotential of 373 mV to achieve the current density of 10 mA cm\n                    <jats:sup>\u22122<\/jats:sup>\n                    in 1.0\n                    <jats:sc>m<\/jats:sc>\n                    phosphate buffer solution, significantly outperforming the commercial IrO\n                    <jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>\n                    catalysts. Further characterizations toward the catalyst after undergoing OER process indicate that unique Co oxyhydroxide and high valence Ir species with low\u2010coordination structure are formed due to the high oxidation potentials, which authentically contributes to superior OER performance. This work not only provides a state\u2010of\u2010the\u2010art OER catalyst in neutral media but also unravels the root of the excellent performance based on efficient structural identifications.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/adma.201707522","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2018,3,25]],"date-time":"2018-03-25T03:21:15Z","timestamp":1521948075000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":312,"title":["Atomic Iridium Incorporated in Cobalt Hydroxide for Efficient Oxygen Evolution Catalysis in Neutral Electrolyte"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"30","author":[{"given":"Youkui","family":"Zhang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"National Synchrotron Radiation Laboratory CAS Center for Excellence in Nanoscience University of Science and Technology of China  Hefei 230029 China"},{"name":"School of National Defense Science and Technology Southwest University of Science and Technology  Mianyang 621010 China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Chuanqiang","family":"Wu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Synchrotron Radiation Laboratory CAS Center for Excellence in Nanoscience University of Science and Technology of China  Hefei 230029 China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5243-3524","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hongliang","family":"Jiang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Synchrotron Radiation Laboratory CAS Center for Excellence in Nanoscience University of Science and Technology of China  Hefei 230029 China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yunxiang","family":"Lin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Synchrotron Radiation Laboratory CAS Center for Excellence in Nanoscience University of Science and Technology of China  Hefei 230029 China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Hengjie","family":"Liu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Synchrotron Radiation Laboratory CAS Center for Excellence in Nanoscience University of Science and Technology of China  Hefei 230029 China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Qun","family":"He","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Synchrotron Radiation Laboratory CAS Center for Excellence in Nanoscience University of Science and Technology of China  Hefei 230029 China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Shuangming","family":"Chen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Synchrotron Radiation Laboratory CAS Center for Excellence in Nanoscience University of Science and Technology of China  Hefei 230029 China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Tao","family":"Duan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of National Defense Science and Technology Southwest University of Science and Technology  Mianyang 621010 China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0585-8519","authenticated-orcid":false,"gi